  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ResNet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 acc. The image-only ResNet50 baseline was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image features may be limiting the fusion quality. Config_039 replaces ResNet50 with the much stronger ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L while keeping all other settings (scVI_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) identical to the best result. This isolates the effect of image encoder quality on multimodal fusion performance. If the image modality is contributing positively (0.713 vs 0.653 RNA-only), a stronger image encoder is the most logical way to push accuracy higher. As the final experiment, this maximizes the chance of beating the current best by exploiting the proven optimal configuration with a single, well-motivated upgrade."
